description:
Show the person interactive UI in this chat: a flat list of 1 to 16 components, drawn top to bottom under your message, with no nesting and no styling. This is the only way to show controls; HTML or JSON in your reply is never drawn.

Write your words in your reply as usual and use show_ui for what the person can press or look at. Each component has an id unique in the call, a type, and the props for that type. Labels and details are plain text, never Markdown or links. A press reaches you as the person's own message, the stored label; live controls report what happened as a hidden note. Ask one thing at a time, and only the newest offer takes an answer once the person writes again.

Components:
- images: Image files from your machine in a grid of one to three columns, each with an optional caption. Use it instead of HTML to lay images out.
  props: {"type":"object","required":["images"],"properties":{"images":{"minItems":1,"maxItems":12,"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","required":["path"],"properties":{"path":{"minLength":1,"maxLength":4096,"type":"string"},"alt":{"minLength":1,"maxLength":200,"type":"string"},"caption":{"minLength":1,"maxLength":200,"type":"string"}}}},"columns":{"anyOf":[{"const":1,"type":"number"},{"const":2,"type":"number"},{"const":3,"type":"number"}]}}}
- choice: Up to six buttons for one question; one may be primary, the step you recommend. A press sends the option's label as the person's message, and the offer closes once answered or once they type.
  props: {"type":"object","required":["options"],"properties":{"options":{"minItems":1,"maxItems":6,"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","required":["id","label"],"properties":{"id":{"minLength":1,"maxLength":64,"type":"string"},"label":{"minLength":1,"maxLength":80,"type":"string"},"primary":{"type":"boolean"}}}}}}
- checklist: Options the person ticks, then submits with submitLabel; `checked` ticks one in advance. The submission reaches you as their message: the submit label and the ticked labels, or emptyLabel when nothing is ticked.
  props: {"type":"object","required":["options","submitLabel"],"properties":{"options":{"minItems":1,"maxItems":32,"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","required":["id","label"],"properties":{"id":{"minLength":1,"maxLength":64,"type":"string"},"label":{"minLength":1,"maxLength":80,"type":"string"},"detail":{"minLength":1,"maxLength":200,"type":"string"},"checked":{"type":"boolean"}}}},"submitLabel":{"minLength":1,"maxLength":80,"type":"string"},"emptyLabel":{"minLength":1,"maxLength":80,"type":"string"}}}
- text_field: A one-field answer, such as a nickname or a repository address. What they type reaches you as their message.
  props: {"type":"object","required":["label","submitLabel"],"properties":{"label":{"minLength":1,"maxLength":80,"type":"string"},"placeholder":{"minLength":1,"maxLength":80,"type":"string"},"submitLabel":{"minLength":1,"maxLength":80,"type":"string"}}}
- file_tree: Paths drawn as a file tree, for showing a project's layout or what changed. Nothing in it is pressable.
  props: {"type":"object","required":["paths"],"properties":{"paths":{"minItems":1,"maxItems":200,"type":"array","items":{"minLength":1,"maxLength":1024,"type":"string"}}}}
- provider_sign_in: One AI's install and sign-in, live: it installs the AI's program when it is missing, opens its own sign-in, and takes a sign-in code or a pasted setup token or API key. Show one per AI the person may connect. A finished sign-in reaches you as a hidden note.
  props: {"type":"object","required":["provider"],"properties":{"provider":{"anyOf":[{"const":"claude","type":"string"},{"const":"codex","type":"string"},{"const":"grok","type":"string"},{"const":"antigravity","type":"string"}]},"target":{"anyOf":[{"const":"team","type":"string"},{"const":"private","type":"string"}]}}}
- default_model: The default model for new conversations, live, with a control that changes it. Show it only when the person asks about models.
  props: {"type":"object","properties":{}}
- phone_app: The codes that download Happy's phone app, to scan with the phone's camera.
  props: {"type":"object","properties":{}}
- phone_pair: This computer's pairing code for Happy on the phone, live: the person scans it in the app and compares the emoji on both screens. A paired phone reaches you as a hidden note.
  props: {"type":"object","properties":{}}
